The reader itself is CarbonEngineJS code in the resource capability of
`@carbonenginejs/runtime`. The Wwise RIFF/RIFX chunk layout and codec-tag
meanings were taken from the community tools ww2ogg, vgmstream and wwiser, and
checked against EVE Online media. No Audiokinetic SDK or binary was used by
this project.

Third-party code
----------------

ww2ogg, by Adam Gashlin (hcs)
Repository: https://github.com/hcs64/ww2ogg
License: BSD 3-clause; full text in format-notices/wem/LICENSE

  Copyright (c) 2002, Xiph.org Foundation
  Copyright (c) 2009-2016, Adam Gashlin

The Wwise Vorbis to Ogg repacker is a JavaScript translation of ww2ogg:
- src/resource/formats/wem/core/wemToOgg.js, from src/wwriff.cpp;
- src/resource/formats/wem/core/codebookLibrary.js, from src/codebook.cpp;
- the OggPageWriter in src/resource/formats/wem/core/bitStream.js, from
  src/Bit_stream.h.
The bundled packed codebook data
(src/resource/formats/wem/core/packedCodebooksAotuv603.js) is a byte-identical
copy of ww2ogg's packed_codebooks_aoTuV_603.bin, which derives from the aoTuV
Vorbis encoder by Aoyumi.

